  "id": "intermodal-matching",
  "term": "intermodal matching",
  "definition": "Intermodal matching is the proposed ability to connect what a person sees another individual do with the motor pattern needed to do the same action themselves, allowing imitation. In this source, it is discussed as part of a theory that such matching could operate automatically from birth.",
